cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below."
title: "valplan: planning tool-using agents by predicate abstraction over a decidable algebra of JSON Schema contracts"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pigazzini
    given-names: Pasquale
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-6977-7317"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.0.1
date-released: "2026-10-27"
abstract: >-
  Plans tool-using agents in which every call is proven well-typed. MCP tool contracts in
  JSON Schema, draft 2020-12 and drafts 07, 06 and 04 through an upgrade, are compiled into
  sets that valgebra decides inclusion and emptiness over; the Boolean algebra those sets
  generate is cut into finitely many cells, and a planner searches the cells for a program
  of tool calls and static type tests on values that reaches the goal whatever values inside
  their output schemas the tools return. A verifier asks valgebra alone, without the cells
  or the search, about every link of a program, one written elsewhere included: each is
  proven, refuted with a value outside it, or left undecided. The compiler passes every case
  it runs of the official JSON-Schema-Test-Suite for drafts 2020-12, 07, 06 and 04, and
  compiles 9301 of the 9558 real-world schemas of JSONSchemaBench with none crashing. Every
  published count is reproduced by a committed command.
repository-code: "https://github.com/ppigazzini/valplan"
keywords:
  - semantic subtyping
  - JSON Schema
  - predicate abstraction
  - planning under nondeterminism
  - program synthesis
  - tool-using agents
  - Model Context Protocol
